<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Dr. King returns three weeks after his preventive visit. The nurse telephone call planned two weeks after starting sertraline did not reach him because he was travelling; he took sertraline 50 mg daily, with nausea for a few days only. He has had six therapy sessions and keeps a fixed rising time; he now sleeps about six hours. He stopped smoking on his quit date two weeks ago, using varenicline, and has mild nausea after the morning dose and vivid dreams, but no change in mood; cravings come late at night when he writes. He has kept his day off on four of the past six weeks. His home blood pressure readings over seven days averaged 136/86. He has had no thoughts of harming himself. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Sertraline</td><td>50 mg for five weeks; early nausea only</td></tr><tr><td>Missed call</td><td>Two-week nurse call did not reach him</td></tr><tr><td>Smoking</td><td>Stopped two weeks ago on varenicline; night cravings</td></tr><tr><td>Home blood pressure</td><td>Seven-day average 136/86</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>About six hours</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

